samir: Heads-up: PR #3567 adds a Rate Limits how-to but the Node example uses the old import path /sdk/node and the linkchecker flagged it. Can someone fix the snippet and add header examples?
olivia: I'll patch it. Plan: update to `@redwood/inference`, add X-Rate-Limit-* handling, plus a tiny backoff pseudo-code. Also note dashboard panel `billing_quota_usage` for ops mapping.
docs-bot: Preview build 3567 ready: https://deploy-preview.redwood-inference/3567 (status: failed linkcheck) :warning:
samir: Minimal Node snippet suggestion:``
js
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
const res = await client.metrics.rateLimits({ window: 'minute' });
const remaining = res.headers['x-rate-limit-remaining'];
if (remaining && Number(remaining) < 10) {
  // gentle backoff
  await sleep(200 * (10 - Number(remaining)));
}
```
olivia: Go snippet also updated to use headers map and show reset parsing. I'll include a one-line note: server uses UTC for window resets.
